 "title": "Register of Deeds",
 "text": "Register of Deeds\nSkip to main content\nHome\nGovernment\nCounty Commission\nCommissioners\nCounty Clerk's Office\nElections\nCounty Attorney's Office\nRegister of Deeds Office\nCounty Treasurer's Office\nSheriff's Office (Opens in new window)\nDepartments\nAdministration\nAppraiser's Office\nBuildings & Grounds\nCommunity Corrections\nCouncil on Aging\nDistrict Court\nEMS\nGIS\nHealth Department\nHuman Resources\nInformation Systems\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Works\nNoxious Weed\nSurvey Office\nTransfer Station\nInformation\nPhone Directory\nCitizen Request Center\nPublic Service Request\nJob Openings\nBid Notices\nTax Sale\nProject Status Updates\nLive Webcam\nFire Districts & Stations Information (Opens in new window)\nAmericans with Disabilities Act Coordinator\nHow Do I?\nContact Us\nPublic Service Request\nCitizen Request Center\nRequest Open Records\n(Opens in new window)\n(Opens in new window)\nSearch Leavenworth County Kansas\nslide 1 of 1\nRegister of Deeds\nTerriLois G. Todd (Opens in new window)\nRegister of Deeds\nPhone\n913 684-0424\n(Opens in new window)\nAddress\n300 Walnut Street\nLeavenworth, KS 66048\n(Opens in new window)\nSub Menu\nRegister of Deeds Office\nBiometric Lien (Self-Imposed)\nRecording Requirements\nDocument Search\nFee Schedule (Opens in new window)\nForms\nProperty Fraud\nUniform Commercial Code (Opens in new window)\nCustomer Survey\nGIS Cemetery Database (Opens in new window)\nSubdivision Codes\nNEW: Notary Fraud Alert\nHome\nGovernment\nRegister of Deeds Office\nRegister of Deeds\nThe Register of Deeds is responsible for the safe keeping and preserving of documents. We record Warranty Deeds, Transfer on Death Deeds, Quit Claim Deeds, Mortgages, Mortgage Releases, Affidavits, Death Certificates, Surveys, Subdivision Plats, Easements, Military Discharges and many more.\nThe Register of Deeds also files financing statements and security agreements on personal property under the uniform commercial code, as well as Federal, State, and Medical liens.\nReal estate documents are recorded and filed of record as soon as they are received by e-filing. Mailed or walked in documents stop recording at 4:30 p.m. and are returned to the customer the next day.\nFor all documents you are recording whether walked into the office or mailed:\nAll information (no blanks) must be completed on your document prior to presenting it in our office.\nThe Notary Public acknowledgement must be correctly executed.\nCorrect payment presented by check (pay to LV CO ROD), MasterCard, Visa, Discover, or cash (do not mail cash). See the Fee Schedule link for the correct amount of recording fees.\nProvide email address and phone for any questions we may have regarding your document.\nProvide a copy of a state issued photo ID if your filing conveys property.\nProvide a self-addressed stamped envelope if you would like the original document returned after recording. Otherwise, a digital copy of your recorded document will be emailed.\nThe following list is observed holidays when the Register of Deeds Office is closed and will not accept e-Recordings:\n2026 Leavenworth County Holiday Schedule |\nThursday |\nJanuary 1 |\nNew Year's Day |\nMonday |\nJanuary 19 |\nMartin Luther King, Jr. |\nMonday |\nFebruary 16 |\nPresidents' Day |\nMonday |\nMay 25 |\nMemorial Day |\nFriday |\nJune 19 |\nJuneteenth |\nFriday |\nJuly 3 |\nIndependence Day |\nMonday |\nSeptember 7 |\nLabor Day |\nMonday |\nOctober 12 |\nColumbus Day |\nWednesday |\nNovember 11 |\nVeterans Day |\nThursday |\nNovember 26 |\nThanksgiving Day |\nFriday |\nNovember 27 |\nThanksgiving |\nThursday |\nDecember 24 |\nChristmas Eve |\nFriday |\nDecember 25 |\nChristmas Day |\nSIGN-UP FOR ALERTS\nSubscribe Now\nShare this page\nShare this page\n×\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.leavenworthcounty.gov/government/register_of_deeds_office/index.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\n(Opens in new window)\nTwitter\n(Opens in new window)\nReddit\n(Opens in new window)\nClose\nCOUNTY HOURS\nMon-Fri: 8:00AM - 5:00PM\nCOUNTY ADDRESS\n300 Walnut Street\nLeavenworth, KS 66048 (Opens in new window)\nCOUNTY DIRECTORY!\nView County Directory!\n© Leavenworth County, KS. All Rights Reserved.\nPowered by revize., (Opens in new window) the Government Website Experts Login\nModal Title\nModal Subtitle\nClose\nRead More",
